      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "There's nothing worse than having your other hand grab the pickup while you're holding the camera....\n\nIt would be nice to have a feature to disable pickups when you have a camera.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-31T16:21:53.227Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Many worlds do not have an option to disable pickups making it increasingly frustrating to relax in some worlds without constantly getting a blue outline around your controller indicating a pickup is in range. In addition, the photo camera buttons are impossible to use without either grabbing it with one hand, moving uncomfortably far from the screen, or locking the camera, as you cannot interact with any buttons (on the camera or in the world) if it is within pickup range.\nA simple toggle in the menu (quick menu or action menu) to disable pickup interactions and a rework of the VRCCam interaction would resolve this. Being able to adjust the pickup range of the VRCCam would be very convenient. There was previously a mod called “Component Toggle” which let you disable pickups, post processing, avatar pedestals, portals, mirrors, and other players camera lenses.",
